# HG2-B (data(D), item 3): `data(To)` is `call(To data)`, and `data()` runs the launch data over itself. A declaration of a
# visible name assigns the existing place, the call's local (no write-back): To\x stays 0 (copied 0, pinned 7) and Self\x
# stays 1 (own 1, pinned 2). The results are written through data\ (rule Б). Observation: explicit writes in sub: observe (#flush-receiver-contract; #call-frame-20261115).
# visible name assigns the existing place, the call's local (no write-back).
# Step 21.7 K2, S3: both `data(To)` and `data()` are the removed form (a data record launched over other data or over
# itself). The property is carried by the structural link: Copy is written in From and launched over From
# (`From\Copy()`); the inner launch is the relay record of To, `To\Echo()`; the former self-launch is `Self\Apply()`,
# whose relay is the sibling record `Self\Mark()`. Every bare write `x := x + 1` is reached and writes the local of
# its launch (#call-frame-20261115): the local is read out by an explicit write right after it (echo_local 1 -- the
# local of To's relay, 0 + 1; mark_local 2 -- the local of Self's relay, 1 + 1), and no source changes: To\x stays 0
# (copied 0) and Self\x stays 1 (own 1).
# Norm: the book #structural-call, #call-frame-20261115.
Observed:
    int: copied 0
    int: own 0
    int: echo_local 0
    int: mark_local 0
end: Observed
To:
    int: x 0
    Echo:
        x := x + 1
        Observed\echo_local := x
    end: Echo
end: To
From:
    int: x 7
    Copy:
        To\Echo()
    end: Copy
end: From
Self:
    int: x 1
    Mark:
        x := x + 1
        Observed\mark_local := x
    end: Mark
    Apply:
        Self\Mark()
    end: Apply
end: Self
Main:
    From\Copy()
    Self\Apply()
    Observed\copied := To\x
    Observed\own := Self\x
